& [Purpose] is inspectable agreement without authority collapse
  + prove representative syntax behavior against the exact checked-in canonical schemas and actual transport forms
  + preserve every known non-syntactic condition as a stable residual record
  + make disagreement missing coverage unimplemented enforcement and exhaustion visible and release blocking

& [AuthorityStack] is ordered and non-substitutive
  + gate_0 faithful byte ingress proves bounded JSON structure duplicate absence and complete consumption
  + gate_1 schema conformance applies one exact canonical Draft 2020-12 document
  + gate_1_peer serde conformance decodes or encodes the actual operation-specific Rust type independently
  + gate_2 optional semantic evaluation applies existing pure Cantor enforcement to a complete fixture
  + gate_3 authority admission remains outside I03
  + no earlier gate implies a later gate

& [PrerequisiteIdentity] is exact
  + I03 baseline commit is 96113bf024b0dd9d50464cbdfb91db1a80aede59
  + I02 bundle is 247809 bytes SHA256 03616F46C4A3C4B7FA4B9D0A668E16FF4B47BA71CB70879B10F1D95157ADCB42
  + generation source is aba99b1431727578679fa0b784ea8261cfd456fb
  + exactly five document root kinds are prepare_input run_input verify_input base_response and preparation_response
  + every document path length digest id dialect direction closure and residual set is reverified before use

& [FaithfulByteIngress] is atomic
  + accept exact bounded UTF-8 bytes and require exactly one complete JSON value plus trailing whitespace only
  + recursively reject duplicate member names before any object becomes authoritative
  + account bytes depth object members array items scalar values and member-name bytes
  + release one FaithfulJsonInstance only after all lexical structural and limit checks pass
  + duplicate malformed trailing depth and limit faults name bounded path offset limit and observed facts where known

& [IndependentValidatorProfile] is closed
  + candidate is exact jsonschema 0.49.2 subject to separate activation review
  + use default-features false and no added feature unless activation proves it necessary
  + set Draft 2020-12 explicitly
  + enable no HTTP HTTPS file environment registry async or caller-supplied external retrieval
  + preflight rejects every non-fragment or unresolved reference before validator construction
  + validate the canonical document against the proper meta-schema separately from compiling it and validating an instance
  + normalize findings by stable instance path schema path rule class and bounded context; engine display text is advisory only

& [SerdeBinding] is actual not simulated
  + prepare_input decodes PrepareRequest from the original exact bytes
  + run_input decodes PreparedRunRequest from the original exact bytes
  + verify_input decodes VerifyRequest from the original exact bytes
  + base_response serializes actual ProcedureToolResponse fixtures in the base-response intended use
  + preparation_response serializes actual ProcedureToolResponse fixtures in the preparation-response intended use
  + input decoding requires complete consumption and output evidence begins from an actual typed value

& [ResidualRegistry] is complete for the selected baseline
  + every record has stable id title subject types covered roots condition class enforcement disposition stage module function severity proof references related residuals and bounded rationale
  + RMS-R01 through RMS-R06 retain stable identity and gain exact record definitions
  + I03-R007 through I03-R020 cover successor capacity authorship boundaries digest validation receipt replay catalogue coordination exact schema argument operation participant lineage transcript result correspondence exact replay and non-capability
  + an activation audit may split a family into finer records but may not omit or silently rename an existing residual
  + every schema residual reference resolves once and every record is indexed by roots types and enforcement
  + registry digest binds profile ordered records and exact I02 bundle digest

& [ResidualEnforcement] is honest
  + enforced names exact present code and executable proof
  + partially_enforced names proven and open portions
  + unimplemented remains a semantic refusal
  + observational records limitations or non-capabilities that syntax cannot prove
  + schema acceptance never changes any residual disposition

& [ConformanceCase] is immutable and root qualified
  + bind case id root direction exact bytes and digest expected ingress schema serde and optional semantic dispositions
  + name applicability rule ids schema paths residual ids family rationale and fixture proof
  + cases are unique and lexical by case id
  + mutations create new case identities rather than silently changing signed expectations

& [Applicability] prevents false comparisons
  + common_schema_serde requires independently applicable schema and serde results
  + byte_ingress_only governs malformed trailing duplicate and byte-limit cases
  + schema_only and serde_only name representation-specific obligations
  + semantic_only requires a complete safe typed fixture
  + observational carries an honesty limitation without acceptance authority

& [RequiredCorpusFamilies] are accounted
  + positive canonical minimum and representative complete cases
  + below at and above each represented numeric string collection and recursive boundary where constructible
  + missing required optional omission explicit null unknown property wrong JSON type wrong enum and wrong tag
  + duplicate member at root and nested object trailing data malformed string and excessive structural input
  + cross-field digest reference replay authority and non-capability residual witnesses through complete safe fixtures where available
  + each family is present not-applicable or deferred with a signed reason; silent absence is a coverage fault

& [Agreement] is narrow
  + compare schema and serde only for an applicable CommonSyntaxClaim
  + both observations must equal the case expectation and each other
  + rejected plus rejected is valid agreement only when both readers actually ran and refused the named rule
  + skipped not-applicable exhausted panic or internal fault never counts as agreement
  + duplicate-key ingress refusal governs even if ordinary typed serde would otherwise accept a collapsed map

& [SemanticEvaluation] is optional per case and mandatory where claimed
  + call only existing pure safe functions on complete coherent fixtures
  + preserve semantic invalid refusal unimplemented exhausted and internal fault separately
  + never infer semantic pass from schema-serde agreement
  + never perform Observer admission provider invocation model execution or external effect

& [Report] is deterministic and inspectable
  + preserve every reader observation expectation mismatch disagreement residual gap coverage gap exhaustion and internal fault
  + sort findings by case id reader rule schema path and finding id
  + bind bundle registry validator corpus and report digests
  + repeat the complete pure evaluation and require byte-equivalent normalized report
  + passed requires zero findings zero uncovered obligations zero dangling residuals and exact repeat

& [Limits] are exact maxima
  + cases 4096 and aggregate corpus bytes 67108864
  + input bytes 16777216 depth 128 object members 65536 array items 65536 scalar values 131072 member-name bytes 4096
  + normalized findings per case 256 and diagnostic characters per finding 1024
  + documents 4194304 bytes bundle 16777216 bytes definitions 256 references 4096 schema depth 64 properties 4096 alternatives 2048 residuals 1024
  + every counter uses checked arithmetic and stops before unbounded accumulation

& [Faults] are closed and atomic
  + stale_bundle stale_document invalid_utf8 malformed_json trailing_data duplicate_key limit_exceeded invalid_meta_schema unresolved_reference external_reference validator_construction schema_rejected serde_rejected semantic_refused unimplemented_residual conformance_disagreement coverage_gap nondeterminism and internal_fault
  + expected reader rejection is an observation rather than a harness fault
  + no partial registry corpus or passed report is released after a prerequisite fault

& [Proof] is multi-layered
  + source and formation hashes
  + exact I02 artifact replay and independent reference rescan
  + focused ingress duplicate depth and limit adversaries
  + validator no-resolution and meta-schema probes
  + positive negative boundary residual coverage and disagreement fixtures
  + repeat-digest proof
  + full locked offline debug release lint docs audit evidence and diff gates after later implementation

& [ActivationPrerequisites] block implementation
  + exact jsonschema dependency resolution and checksum
  + default-features false tree proving no HTTP file TLS async or runtime retrieval surface
  + complete offline cache and cargo metadata audit
  + Rust 1.96 and Windows Application Control compile execution probe
  + numeric boundary probe below at above u64 maximum without globally enabling arbitrary precision by assumption
  + exact source-touch dependency and rollback lock

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + formation adds only preserved source SJS canonical exploded requirements plan justification review proof narrative and evidence metadata
  - never: Cargo Rust JSON fixture parser validator execution semantic operation compatibility provider model service persistence network external effect production release hardware or FPGA

